  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the mapped divergence:\n\n**Babel side** (`babel--v7.24.0`):\n- `packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts` \u2014 the decision point: `legacy || version === \"legacy\"` routes to the legacy visitor; anything else (including no option, which defaults via `plugin-syntax-decorators` to `\"2018-09\"`, or explicit `\"2023-11\"`) routes to `createClassFeaturePlugin` (stage-3/TC39 form).\n- `transformer-legacy.ts` \u2014 the legacy (stage-2, TS-`experimentalDecorators`-compatible) transform. Critically, it emits **no** `Reflect.metadata`/`design:type` calls at all \u2014 Babel's legacy decorators plugin only rewrites the decorator call sites, never type metadata.\n- `plugin-syntax-decorators/src/index.ts` \u2014 resolves `legacy`/`version`/`decoratorsBeforeExport`, and is what `preset-typescript`-based pipelines inherit ahead of `plugin-transform-typescript`.\n- `plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` \u2014 strips TS type annotations/`TSParameterProperty` in its own `Class` visitor but never touches `node.decorators`; ordering with the decorators plugin only matters for whether type annotations survive long enough for a metadata-emitting plugin to read them (Babel itself doesn't read them \u2014 see below).\n- `helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/decorators.ts` \u2014 the stage-3 (2023-11) implementation used for every non-legacy `version`.\n\n**SWC side** (`swc--v1.4.6`):\n- `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` \u2014 wires `.swcrc`'s `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` \u2192 `decorators::Config.legacy` and `decoratorMetadata` \u2192 `.emit_metadata`; when not legacy, wires to `decorator_2022_03()` instead.\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs` \u2014 the SWC decision point, structurally mirroring Babel's: `legacy: true` \u2192 `legacy::new(emit_metadata)`; `legacy: false` with `emit_metadata: true` \u2192 **`unimplemented!()` panic** (\"emitting decorator metadata while using new proposal\").\n- `decorators/legacy/mod.rs` + `decorators/legacy/metadata.rs` \u2014 SWC's legacy/TSC-compatible path, which (unlike Babel) **natively** emits `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` via `_ts_metadata` calls, but only when `self.metadata` (i.e. `decoratorMetadata: true`) is set \u2014 and only reachable through the `legacy: true` branch. The metadata.rs file's own doc comment credits `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata` as its model.\n\n**The divergence**: Babel's legacy-decorator transform never emitted DI metadata itself \u2014 customers relying on Nest.js typically added the third-party `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata` package alongside `legacy: true`. SWC ported that exact metadata-serialization logic in-tree, but gated it behind **both** `legacyDecorator: true` **and** `decoratorMetadata: true`. If the customer's `.swcrc` only sets one (or neither \u2014 e.g. left `legacyDecorator` at its default `false`), classes still construct (decorators still fire as plain function calls), but no `Reflect.metadata('design:paramtypes', ...)` is ever attached, so Nest's `Reflect.getMetadata` returns `undefined` and DI resolution fails exactly as reported. Setting `decoratorMetadata: true` without `legacyDecorator: true` is even worse \u2014 it hits the `unimplemented!()` panic in `decorators/mod.rs` at compile time in Rust-level testing, though the JS-facing config layer may silently drop metadata emission depending on how the binding surfaces that error.",
